From 05136c7e32923187b68e7a762eacf726e2601db7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mate Soos <soos.mate@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:22:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix assertion failure when the first learnt clauses have LBD
 0

Bug: with -rh lbd, update_lbd_restart_vals() asserts that both moving
averages of learnt-clause LBDs are positive. A clause learnt on decision
level 0 has LBD 0, so when the first conflicts all happen there, both
averages are still exactly 0 and Debug builds abort with

  solver.hpp:1203: update_lbd_restart_vals: Assertion
  `forcing_fast>0 && forcing_slow>0' failed.

(at the very first conflict: lbd=0, s.no_confl=1). Release builds are not
affected beyond not restarting until the first conflict above level 0.

Fix: assert that the averages are non-negative.

Found by differential fuzzing (xnf_fuzzer.py) with a sanitizer build, on a
48-variable 2-XNF instance with
  -dh vsids -po save_inv -rh lbd -delh util -il 0 -ip full -pp no -no-eq
whose answer, UNSAT, the release build gets right.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/solver.hpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/solver.hpp b/src/solver.hpp
index ec3ac12..1b14da4 100644
--- a/src/solver.hpp
+++ b/src/solver.hpp
@@ -1200,7 +1200,8 @@ class solver
         blocking_mult = linear_smoothing * blocking_mult_high + (1-linear_smoothing) * blocking_mult_low;
       }
 
-      assert(forcing_fast>0 && forcing_slow>0);
+      //clauses learnt on dl 0 have LBD 0, so both averages stay 0 until the first conflict above dl 0
+      assert(forcing_fast>=0 && forcing_slow>=0);
 
       VERB(60, "c lbd: " << std::to_string(lbd) << " forcing_fast: " << forcing_fast << " forcing_slow: " << forcing_slow << " blocking: " << blocking);
     }
